  "Is it safe to eat street food?": "吃街头小吃安全吗？",
  "Generally yes, if you choose stalls with good hygiene and high turnover. Look for locals eating there - if they are healthy, it is usually fine. Avoid food that has been sitting out.": "一般来说是安全的，只要选择卫生条件好、客流大的摊位。看看当地人在哪里吃——如果他们吃了没事，通常就没问题。避免食用放置已久的食物。",
  "Do I need to tip in China?": "在中国需要给小费吗？",
  "No, tipping is not expected and not common in local restaurants. Some upscale international restaurants may add a service charge.": "不需要，本地餐厅不期望也不常见给小费。一些高档国际餐厅可能会加收服务费。",
  "What if I cannot eat spicy food?": "如果我吃不了辣怎么办？",
  "Say \"bù yào là\" (no spice) when ordering. Most restaurants can accommodate mild or no spice. Sichuan cuisine may still have some peppercorn flavor even without chili.": "点餐时说“不要辣”。大多数餐厅可以做到微辣或不辣。川菜即使不放辣椒，可能仍有一些花椒味。",
  "How much should I budget for food?": "餐饮预算应该准备多少？",
  "Street food: 20-50 CNY/day, Casual restaurants: 50-150 CNY/meal, Mid-range: 100-300 CNY/meal, High-end: 500+ CNY/meal. Prices vary by city.": "街头小吃：每天20-50元；普通餐厅：每餐50-150元；中档餐厅：每餐100-300元；高档餐厅：每餐500元以上。价格因城市而异。",
  "Ordering": "点餐",
